@startuml
title CDN Peering Lifecycle

start

:Publish resource and service information to Service Registry;
if (Is peering initiation needed due to hotspot or exceptional load, including expected and unexpected load increases?) then (hotspot/exceptional load with expected and unexpected load increases)
:Send initialization request to mediator;
:Mediator obtains resource/access info from SR and policy info from PR and generates service requirements;
if (Are service requirements acceptable under provider policy?) then (acceptable)
:Pass service requirements to local Peering Agent;
if (Do preexisting peering policies or arrangements exist?) then (preexisting policies exist)
:Return preexisting peering policies and proceed with long-term peering arrangement;
:Establish peering arrangement;
:Configure CDN peering protocols and advertise CDN configuration information;
:Exchange content availability information and support request redirection to an optimal peer;
:Deploy and administer functional policies; exchange accounting information for billing;
repeat
repeat while (arrangement remains valid and beneficial) is (true)
:Disband or re-arrange peering arrangement through renegotiation;
else (no preexisting policies exist)
:Perform short-term negotiation and inter-PA communication to discover external resources;
repeat
repeat while (insufficient resources acquired) is (true)
endif
else (rejected)
endif
else (no)
:Replicate content on-demand from origin server and store it for future use;
:Ensure delivery of content to end-users based on negotiated policies;
:Determine delegable resources and delegation conditions with mediator and reserve/provision resources for SLAs;
:Measure, report, and disseminate load information hierarchically;
endif

stop

@enduml